{
  "file": "mobile.musa",
  "tokens": [
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Stockhausen's Klavierstück XI is nineteen fragments on one large sheet: the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// pianist looks away, looks back, and plays whichever fragment their eye lands" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// on, until the sheet has been crossed three times. This file is that *shape* —" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// the fragments are written for musa, not transcribed — and it is here because" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// nineteen fragments have 19! orderings, which is the number that settled the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// argument in `docs/kernel/11-realization.md`: a finite `choose` cannot hold" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// them, and a permutation costs nineteen `u32`s." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//     musa kernel examples/mobile.musa --seed 7" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The same seed is the same reading, every time; a different seed is a" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// different one. That is law R1, and it is what makes a mobile a piece a" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// recording can be made of rather than a lottery." },
    { "kind": "piece", "text": "piece" },
    { "kind": "string", "text": "\"Nineteen\"" },
